diff --git a/doc/services/storage/file_system/index.rst b/doc/services/storage/file_system/index.rst
--- a/doc/services/storage/file_system/index.rst
+++ b/doc/services/storage/file_system/index.rst
@@ -44,6 +44,27 @@ where
 
 
 
+tmpfs
+*****
+
+:kconfig:option:`CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_TMPFS` provides ``FS_TMPFS``, a file system
+that lives entirely in pages mapped on demand: its nodes, the contents of its
+files and its own bookkeeping come from :c:func:`k_mem_map` on targets with an
+MMU and from page-aligned heap blocks elsewhere, one
+:kconfig:option:`CONFIG_TMPFS_PAGE_SIZE` at a time. No device is involved: a
+mount starts empty and unmounting releases every page. Files, directories,
+symbolic links (followed on lookup, read with :c:func:`fs_readlink`) and FIFO
+nodes are supported; a page is only allocated for a part of a file that has
+been written, so a sparse file costs what it holds. A mount needs nothing
+but a mount point:
+
+.. code-block:: c
+
+	static struct fs_mount_t tmp = {
+		.type = FS_TMPFS,
+		.mnt_point = "/tmp",
+	};
+
 Samples
 *******
 
